<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#hand-cannon">Glossary</a> · Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hand cannon</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as hand cannons</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The hand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> was an early firearm consisting of a simple metal tube fired by igniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">gunpowder</a> by hand. It developed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and spread widely in the fourteenth and fifteenth centuries. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> equipped its armies with hand cannons as part of its large-scale use of gunpowder weapons.</p></div>
